 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Quality Gates (Thresholds)
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`).
+- Each threshold is evaluated: pass if metric score >= minimum, fail if score < minimum or metric has no score.
+- Reports include a `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array listing each threshold's result.
+- CLI `--threshold <metric>=<min>` flags can be repeated; exit code 1 if any fail, 2 for format/validation errors.
+- Works for custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` and supports future metric plug-ins.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
